// The first Harrowmere, sunk into a cavern under the town that was raised on its ruins: below the Sodden
// Pall's cistern its wall gives way onto a sheer chasm, the drowned city standing in it in tiers. From
// the Breach Landing the Cliff Stair winds down the north wall to the bell-keepers' terrace; a bridge
// runs out to the Bell Tower, its stair winding down round the tower's core to the Aqueduct, which
// carries you west to the Colonnade. From there the Grand Stair goes down to the Drowned Plaza, under a
// great rift of daylight in the cavern's vault far overhead, falls of water pouring from the vault's
// fissures past it into the chasm. Below the plaza, across the masons'
// two roads of light (only one standing at a time; a ward crystal swaps them), the Keystone, the giant
// the first city was raised on, lies in its Foundation Court; behind it a lift
// climbs the old gallery's shaft back up to its door in the landing's south wall; a false wall in
// that gallery hides the Bell-keepers' Oubliette. Stone Golems stand like statues until you come
// close, and the Sunken Sextons toll through their mortar-light staves to wake them. Over it all
// hangs the vault of the cavern, rough rock 24 m up with stalactites hanging from it (`vault`), the rift (`sun_shaft`) in it.
// Below the Oubliette the gaolers' stair runs down to the Under-Cells; east of the roads of light the
// Mortar Sisters' Workshop stands on its quay, and a third, teal road (fed from the mortar-light in the
// plaza's fountain) runs home from the core's shield ward.

